      "text": "To determine the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) such that the quadratic polynomial \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we start by expressing the polynomial in the form:\n\n\\[\n(x - p)(x - q) = x^2 - (p+q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nThis transformation reveals that the product of the binomials must equal 2008. Therefore, we set up the equation:\n\n\\[\npq = 2008\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the integer pairs \\((p, q)\\) such that \\( pq = 2008 \\) and then identify the pairs that will give the smallest positive value of \\( b = p + q \\).\n\nFirst, we factorize 2008 to find its pairs:\n\n\\[\n2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n\\]\n\nThe prime factorization of 2008 provides us with all the possible values for \\( p \\) and \\( q \\):\n\n\\[\n(p, q) = (1, 2008), (-1, -2008), (2, 1004), (-2, -1004), (4, 502), (-4, -502), (8, 251), (-8, -251)\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( b = p + q \\) for each pair:\n\n1. For (1, 2008):\n\\[\nb = 1 + 2008 = 2009\n\\]\n\n2. For (-1, -2008):\n\\[\nb = -1 - 2008 = -2009\n\\]\n\n3. For (2, 1004):\n\\[\nb = 2 + 1004 = 1006\n\\]\n\n4. For (-2, -1004):\n\\[\nb = -2 - 1004 = -1006\n\\]\n\n5. For (4, 502):\n\\[\nb = 4 + 502 = 506\n\\]\n\n6. For (-4, -502):\n\\[\nb = -4 - 502 = -506\n\\]\n\n7. For (8, 251):\n\\[\nb = 8 + 251 = 259\n\\]\n\n8. For (-8, -251):\n\\[\nb = -8 - 251 = -259\n\\]\n\nAmong these values, the smallest positive value of \\( b \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
